I looked into this issue and here is a structured fix proposal covering all 4 problems:

1. Infinite WebSocket reconnect loop (DirectTerminal.tsx)
- Add capped retries (e.g., 8 attempts)
- Use exponential backoff
- Stop reconnecting once session is exited

Pseudo:
let retries = 0;
const MAX_RETRIES = 8;

function connect() {
  if (retries >= MAX_RETRIES) {
    setError("Connection failed");
    return;
  }

  const ws = new WebSocket(url);

  ws.onclose = () => {
    if (sessionExited) return;
    retries++;
    setTimeout(connect, Math.min(1000 * 2 ** retries, 10000));
  };
}

2. SSE crash fix (/api/events/route.ts)
- Guard enqueue with closed flag

let closed = false;

return new ReadableStream({
  start(controller) {
    emitter.on("event", (data) => {
      if (!closed) controller.enqueue(data);
    });
  },
  cancel() {
    closed = true;
  }
});

3. WebSocket close code fix (direct-terminal-ws.ts)
- Replace 1008 with custom code 4004

ws.close(4004, "Session not found");

4. UI fix (SessionDetail.tsx)
- Prevent terminal mount if session exited

if (session.status === "exited") {
  return <div className="p-4 text-sm text-gray-500">Session ended</div>;
}

Optional improvements:
- Use AbortController for SSE cleanup
- Persist retry count using useRef
- Show retry state in UI for better UX

