## ⚠️ Regression Analysis: Orchestrator Sessions Being Killed + New Sessions Failing

After deeper investigation, I've identified the root causes of the regression where orchestrator sessions are being killed and new sessions can't open.

---

### Root Cause 1: Orchestrator Session Recognition Regression (sessions being killed)

**File:** `packages/core/src/session-manager.ts` — `isOrchestratorSessionRecord()`

The `endsWith("-orchestrator")` safety net was removed:

```typescript
// OLD — catches all orchestrator-named sessions
if (raw["role"] === "orchestrator" || sessionId.endsWith("-orchestrator")) return true;

// NEW — only matches role metadata or specific prefix patterns
if (raw["role"] === "orchestrator") return true;
if (sessionPrefix) {
  if (sessionId === `${sessionPrefix}-orchestrator`) return true;
  return new RegExp(`^${escapeRegex(sessionPrefix)}-orchestrator-\\d+$`).test(sessionId);
}
return false;  // ← No fallback
```

**Impact:** Existing orchestrator sessions that don't yet have `role: orchestrator` stamped in metadata AND don't match the specific prefix pattern are now treated as **regular worker sessions** — eligible for cleanup and kill. The role-backfill read-repair (`repairSingleSessionMetadataOnRead`) also uses this same function now, so it can't repair sessions it doesn't recognize either, creating a vicious cycle.

---

### Root Cause 2: `storageKey` Undefined → Session Invisibility (new sessions can't open)

**File:** `packages/core/src/session-manager.ts` — `list()`, `get()`, `spawn()`

```typescript
// list() silently skips projects without storageKey
if (!project.storageKey) return [];

// get() silently skips
if (!project.storageKey) continue;

// paths.ts — crashes on spawn/any path resolution
function requireStorageKey(storageKey: string | undefined): string {
  if (!storageKey) throw new Error("storageKey is required");
}
```

If `storageKey` isn't populated (flat config without global config, migration failure, or `ProjectResolveError`):
- `list()` returns empty → dashboard shows no sessions
- `spawn()` crashes with "storageKey is required"
- New sessions cannot be created

The migration path via `applyWrappedLocalStorageKeys()` only runs for "wrapped" config shapes. Flat local configs that go through `buildEffectiveConfigFromFlatLocalPath()` depend on the global config having the project registered — if it doesn't, `storageKey` is never set.

---

### Root Cause 3: Lifecycle Manager Cache Invalidation Removed (contributing)

**File:** `packages/core/src/lifecycle-manager.ts` ~line 723

`sessionManager.invalidateCache()` was removed after the lifecycle manager writes PR metadata. The session cache serves stale data for up to 35s, causing lifecycle decisions on outdated state.

---

### Recommended Fixes

1. **Restore the `endsWith("-orchestrator")` fallback** in `isOrchestratorSessionRecord` when `sessionPrefix` is unavailable — this is the safety net that prevents killing orchestrator sessions
2. **Ensure `storageKey` is always derived** — `applyProjectDefaults()` should generate a storageKey using the legacy `generateConfigHash(configPath) + "-" + projectId` pattern when one isn't set, rather than leaving it undefined
3. **Restore `sessionManager.invalidateCache()`** in lifecycle-manager after metadata writes
4. **Guard `spawn()`** — derive storageKey on the fly if undefined instead of crashing

The combination of (1) and (2) explains both symptoms: existing orchestrator sessions get killed because they're no longer recognized, and new sessions can't open because the storage path can't be resolved.

## Root Cause Analysis

**Reported by:** @harshitsingh in [Discord](https://discord.com/channels/1491735678156013588/1495785851597226045)
**Date:** 2026-04-21
**Analyzed against:** `f3ce113c` (main HEAD)

### The actual bug

The mobile kanban override at `@media (max-width: 767px)` in `globals.css` (~L5358) sets:

```css
.kanban-board {
  flex-direction: column;  /* ← THIS DOES NOTHING */
  height: auto;
  min-height: auto;
  overflow-x: visible;
  gap: 12px;
}
```

But the **base** `.kanban-board` style (~L4622) is:

```css
.kanban-board {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
  ...
}
```

**`flex-direction` has no effect on a `display: grid` container.** The 5-column grid persists on mobile — columns get squeezed to ~20% viewport width each, causing all the truncation, overflow, and crowding issues visible in the screenshot.

### Which PR broke it

**PR #927** (`af2af115` — "style(design): design review fixes + fresh Warm Terminal design system", merged 2026-04-11, by @ashish921998) **changed `.kanban-board` from `display: flex` to `display: grid`** but did not update the mobile override. The mobile override was written for flexbox (from `8fc778cf` — the original mobile-responsive commit) and has been broken since #927 merged.

PR #1278 ("terminal layout, mobile UX, sidebar & instant session navigation") touched `globals.css` extensively but did not touch the kanban board CSS, so it never fixed this.

### Fix

The mobile override needs to switch from `flex-direction: column` to proper grid stacking:

```css
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .kanban-board {
    display: flex;           /* switch back to flex for mobile */
    flex-direction: column;  /* now this actually works */
    height: auto;
    min-height: auto;
    overflow-x: visible;
    gap: 12px;
  }
}
```

Or alternatively, keep grid and override the columns:

```css
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .kanban-board {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;  /* single column on mobile */
  }
}
```

Either approach works. The `display: flex` switch is cleaner since the existing flex-based overrides (`flex: none`, `width: 100%`, etc.) on `.kanban-column` all assume flexbox.

