Superseded by the final implementation in #3548.

The initial design below described four-provider switching and durable deterministic `handoff.md`/`handoff.json` artifacts. That is no longer the implemented contract.

The final first release:

- supports switching only between Claude Code and Codex;
- keeps AO-derived deterministic switch context in memory;
- persists only the optional source-authored `agent-handoff.json` when one is safely received;
- passes a verified read-only native transcript path and a bounded recent-history fallback to the target;
- never creates `prepared.*` or deterministic `handoff.*` files;
- never rewrites provider-native JSON/JSONL session history.

The current contract and verification are documented in the PR description for #3548.

Implementation is now available as draft PR #3548:

https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3548

It implements the design discussed above for the initial provider set: Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and Kimi.

Highlights:

- preserves the AO session, worktree, branch, task, PR, browser, and terminal surface;
- stores provider-native resume references separately from the durable switch saga;
- creates a deterministic handoff artifact with optional source-agent enrichment;
- reuses a native provider session only with positive provider-specific evidence;
- never rewrites or materializes provider JSON/JSONL transcripts;
- generation-fences source stop, target activation, hooks, terminal input, delivery acknowledgement, and crash recovery;
- exposes the flow through the daemon API, CLI, and desktop UI.

The implementation-aligned design document is included here:

https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/blob/codex/agent-switching/docs/agent-switching.md

